>> title: Crispy Chickpea Bowl
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: chickpeas, quinoa, carrots, zaatar, vegetarian, sheet pan, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: crispy chickpea bowl, roasted chickpea bowl, chickpea crunch bowl, quinoa bowl, vegetarian bowl, grain bowl, power bowl, buddha bowl
>> pairs-with: zaatar, tahini-sauce, hummus
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.1: Chickpeas only crisp if they are dry. Drain them an hour ahead if you can, roll them in a towel and rub the loose skins off — the skins are what go leathery in the oven.
>> step.2: toast 3 min, simmer 15 min, rest 10 min
>> step.3: roast 425°F (220°C) 35 min, until they rattle
>> step.4: spice them hot
>> step.5: roast 425°F (220°C) 28 min, cut side down
>> step.6: build it, chickpeas last so they stay loud

Chickpeas only crisp if they are dry. Drain them an hour ahead if you can, roll them in a towel and rub the loose skins off — the skins are what go leathery in the oven.

Toast @quinoa{1%cup}(170 g; rinsed and drained well) dry in a #saucepan{} ~toast{3%min}, until it smells nutty, then simmer it covered with @water{1 3/4%cups}(415 mL) and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} ~simmer{15%min}, and ~rest{10%min} off the heat.

Roast @chickpeas{2%cans}(15 oz each; drained, dried, loose skins rubbed off) tossed with @olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} on a #sheet pan{} at 425°F (220°C) ~roast{35%min}, shaking the pan twice, until they rattle and crack under a thumb.

Toss @&(~1)chickpeas{} hot with @za'atar{1%Tbs} — the heat left in them is what makes the spice stick instead of sitting in the bottom of the pan.

Roast @carrots{1%lb}(450 g; halved lengthwise) tossed with @olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @honey{1%Tbs} and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} at 425°F (220°C) ~roast{28%min}, cut side down, until the flat faces caramelise.

Fork @&(~4)quinoa{} into four bowls, lay @&(~1)roasted carrots{} over it and scatter @&(~2)za'atar chickpeas{} across the top, then finish with @baby kale{4%cups}(packed), @tahini sauce{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @lemon{1/2}(juiced) and @flat-leaf parsley{1/4%cup}(chopped).
